<section class="logging-guide" aria-labelledby="logging-title">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Google Sheets workflow</p>
        <h2 id="logging-title">How to add a reading</h2>
        <p class="public-note">
            Notes appear on this public page. Keep private details and precise home-location
            information out of the sheet.
        </p>
    </div>
    <ol>
        <li>
            Open <strong>Quick log</strong> and find the permanent row for this plant. The P-number
            remains stable even if its physical pot label changes.
        </li>
        <li>
            Fill only what you checked. Weight, height, width, watering, and condition do not need
            to happen together.
        </li>
        <li>
            Enter the measured weight without choosing a dry or wet state. The logger saves it as{" "}
            <code>Routine</code>; applicable cycle comparisons are derived from recorded watering.
            Pending terrarium identities and setup require manual care review.
        </li>
        <li>
            Tick <strong>Save</strong>. The logger appends one or more event-specific History rows
            and clears the input fields; older readings are never overwritten.
        </li>
        <li>
            In the mobile logger, <strong>Repot</strong> records the old and new pot size and
            advances <code>Pot setup</code>
            automatically. Setup 1 means the first tracked whole-pot configuration—not a 1-inch pot.
        </li>
    </ol>
</section>
